<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n66771" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεταλλ-εύω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>get by mining</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χαλκόν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>De.</u>
					8.9
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χρυσοῖο γενέθλην</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.P.
					1114
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be got by mining</i>, of metals, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				288d
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				378a27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1258b32
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>abs.,
			<i>mine</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ μεταλλεύοντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					<u>Bel.</u>
					99.13
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				5.37
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Cont.</u>
				11
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λαμψακηνοῖς μ.</span>
			<i>work in mines</i> for the L., <i><span class="en">
				Polyaen.
				2.1.26
			</span></i> (-<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ηνοί</span> codd., i. e. <i>condemn
				to labour in mines</i>): c. acc. cogn., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πᾶν μεταλλεύων γνύθος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Lyc.
					485
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>carry on mining operations</i>, of besiegers, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				18.70
			</span></i>: also c. acc. cogn., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. τὰς ὑπονόμους σήραγγας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					4.44
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Polyaen.
				7.11.5
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b>
			<i>undermine</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τείχη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>AJ</u>
					17.10.3
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>5.</b>
			<i>explore,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				AP
				6.302
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				672
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μ. τὴν ἔρευναν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Porph.
					<u>Marc.</u>
					26
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μεταλλάσσω</span>
			, <i>pervert</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥεμβασμὸς ἐπιθυμίας μ. νοῦν ἄκακον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					LXX
					<u>Wi.</u>
					4.12
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be converted</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς
				πάντα</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				16.25
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
